        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Staining a concrete patio is mostly preparation. Choose a stain that matches the look you want, make sure the slab is old enough and bare enough for water to soak in, clean and etch it properly, and test a hidden patch all the way through to the sealer before you colour the whole thing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then apply in small sections out of direct sun, neutralise and rinse if you used acid stain, and seal with two thin coats. Follow the label cure times before moving furniture back, and your patio will hold its colour for years with nothing more than a periodic recoat of sealer.
          </p>
        </div>

